CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ lvalue vs rvalue reference: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
static assertion failed
--
A partial specialization of a variable template, same_v<T, T>, matched
same_v<int &&, int &>: irept equality ignores the attributes that tell
lvalue from rvalue references.  The MSVC STL's std::is_same is built on
such a variable template (cpp11_is_same_reference_kinds on Windows).
